<!--
  mutation-test.xml — scopes mutation_test (https://pub.dev/packages/mutation_test)
  to the TDD code introduced by feature 041-tdd-setup-plugin. Per `.specify/
  memory/tdd-profile.md` the mutation phase is now wired (no longer a "spot
  check" fallback).

  Why a config file (not `dart run mutation_test` with no args):
    - The default invocation mutates ALL of `lib/`, which is ~120 source
      files. Per-mutant we run `dart test test/cli/writers/tdd/ test/plugins/tdd/`
      (~0.9s). At ~5 mutants per file this would take hours and would not
      fit the rubric's "<10s per mutant" budget for this PR scope.
    - Scoping to the 21 TDD files (writers + plugin + tdd_command aggregator)
      gives a focused audit of the code the spec 041 introduces, which is
      the honest answer to "are the new tests strong enough to catch
      regressions in the new code?".

  The full-suite mutation audit is intentionally deferred: the spec 041
  acceptance criteria (US9.AC1–3) only require `zfa tdd verify` to emit a
  coverage + mutation audit for the feature under test, not the whole repo.

  Run:    dart run mutation_test mutation-test.xml -f md -o mutation-test-report
  Output: mutation-test-report/mutation-test.md (+ html)
-->
<mutations version="1.0">
  <files>
    <file>lib/src/cli/writers/tdd/dart_test_yaml_writer.dart</file>
